   Two suggestions :

 (a) All religions, more or less, seem to maintain the polarity of
     God and Demon.  Why not keep altars for Demon (Satan ?) as well!
     The player gets different types of weapons depending on who 
     he chooses.  The idea of conflict between God and Demon is always
     more appealing than between two Gods (at the time of altar 
     conversion).  

     Keep differences like :

	Demon class :
	   get weapons like Stormy 
	   but no ability to get holy water

	God class :
	    no weapon like Stormy
	    


   
        There will be monsters which belong to one of these classes

	   Demon class monster is particularly a pleasing sacrifice to
	   God and vice versa.



  (b) The idea of Ghosts is great.  What is lacking with them is the 
      ability to fight.  Even a great fighters Ghost is wimpy. Takes
      only a hit point per shot.  

      When reading about soldiers in the hell, I got this idea :

     (these soldies are supposed to be hackers who were controlled by
      the wizard's magic !!).

	Why not (with a 30% chance, say) this really happen to the 
      real hackers ?  Why not keep a guy in Wizard's control instead
      of killing himn and leave the Ghost ?  That way, we will face
      other hackers whose ability chances from game to game. 

       This leaves hack a more challenging game because now we can 
       face monsters of a variety of abilities.  

       If a hacker dies with the spell of polymorph, he can polymorph you.
       If he knows the spell of magic missile, he can use magic missiles.
	He can use his wands.  Read scrolls to enchant weapon or armor.
	He can throw potions of paralysis ,  ...
       I think the changes possible are only limited by imagination.


        Of course, if you can tame a strong character, it can work in your
        favor and against the wizard.

      
What do you think ?



